    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hi, I'm reviewing our HACCP plan for our catering kitchen. Can you give me the specific temperature and time requirements for the cooling phase of cooked poultry? I need to make sure we're preventing Clostridium perfringens growth correctly.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For cooked poultry, the cooling phase must reduce the food temperature from 135°F (57°C) to 70°F (21°C) within 2 hours, and then from 70°F to 41°F (5°C) or lower within an additional 4 hours. This total cooling period must not exceed 6 hours to prevent Clostridium perfringens growth. Always document these specific time and temperature controls in your HACCP plan to ensure compliance.",
